      </div>
      <p>On October 15, the day after OpenEvidence filed that opposition, the parties filed a Joint Notice of Settlement: "Have reached a settlement in principle." The stipulation of dismissal followed the next day. Rule 41(a)(1)(A)(ii). All claims and counterclaims dismissed with prejudice. Each party to bear its own costs and attorneys' fees. Three law firms signed: Quinn Emanuel for OpenEvidence, Skadden Arps for Doximity and Pathway, Morrison & Foerster for the individual Pathway defendants.</p>
      <p>The settlement terms were not disclosed.</p>
      <p>One loose thread: Eric Yamga, named as a defendant in the amended complaint and described as "a former employee or agent of Pathway Medical," is absent from both the Joint Notice of Settlement and the Stipulation of Dismissal. The record does not explain his status.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="signal">
      <h2><span class="num">05 — Signal</span>The Question Without an Answer</h2>
      <p>The case resolved nothing on the merits. Every substantive legal question it raised — whether prompt injection can constitute trade-secret theft, whether extracting a system prompt violates the CFAA, whether NPI-based access to a non-public AI tier is "without authorization" — ended unanswered. Dismissed with prejudice means these parties cannot relitigate. It creates no precedent for anyone else.</p>
      <p>What the docket shows, structurally: the computer-fraud claim that survived a motion to dismiss rested on alleged fraud at the point of access. The contract claim that survived rested on terms of use the defendants allegedly accepted, which OpenEvidence said they broke by registering falsely, using the platform for commercial purposes and failing to respect confidential information. None of the surviving claims asked the court to decide whether the prompts themselves were theft. Whether a system prompt can be a trade secret was argued by Doximity and never tested by the court.</p>
      <p>No other US case was identified in the course of reporting this story, outside the OpenEvidence litigation family, that has pleaded prompt extraction as trade-secret theft. This is a statement about what was found, not a claim about what exists.</p>
      <p>The open question is structural. If the computer-fraud theory that survived was about fraud at the login, then what about everyone who logs in honestly? A credentialed physician, an authorized API integration, a legitimate contractor — they sit inside the gate the law cared about. The words they type into the prompt box were never the subject of a ruling. Every deployed system prompt sits behind whatever gate its operator built. In this case, the hacking theory that survived was about lying to get through that gate. For someone who walks through it honestly, what is left is a terms-of-use contract.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</StoryLayout>

<script>
(function () {
  const canvas = document.querySelector('.openevidence-doximity-prompt-injection-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  if (!canvas) return;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  if (!ctx) return;

  // --- Read CSS custom properties ---
  const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
  const bgColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--bg').trim() || '#0d0d0d';
  const storyColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--story').trim() || '#0891b2';

  // --- Parse story color to RGB ---
  function hexToRgb(hex: string): [number, number, number] {
    const h = hex.replace('#', '');
    return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];
  }
  const [sr, sg, sb] = hexToRgb(storyColor);

  function accentA(a: number): string { return `rgba(${sr},${sg},${sb},${a})`; }
  function dimA(a: number): string { return `rgba(232,232,232,${a})`; }
  function clamp(v: number, lo: number, hi: number): number { return v < lo ? lo : v > hi ? hi : v; }

  // --- State ---
  let W = 0, H = 0, rafId = 0, frame = 0;
  const prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  // --- Phase thresholds (~22s at 60fps = ~1320 frames) ---
  const P1_END = 120;   // calm: authorized particles drift
  const P2_END = 200;   // approach: bare particle enters, absorbs credential
  const P3_END = 260;   // crossing: particle crosses threshold, flare
  const P4_END = 380;   // tendrils: disguised particle reaches core
  const P5_END = 480;   // dissolve: tendrils vanish, core dims, threshold grows
  const P6_END = 600;   // hold: threshold dominates, interior dark
  const P7_END = 660;   // fade out
  const CYCLE = 660;

  // --- Authorized particles (6 physicians in right zone) ---
  const AUTH_COUNT = 6;
  interface AuthParticle {
    x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number; alpha: number;
    orbitAngle: number; orbitSpeed: number;
  }
  const authParticles: AuthParticle[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
    authParticles.push({ x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, alpha: 0.06, orbitAngle: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2, orbitSpeed: 0.015 + Math.random() * 0.01 });
  }

  // --- Intruder particle ---
  const intruder = { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0.4, vy: 0, hasCredential: false, orbitAngle: 0, alpha: 0 };

  // --- Credential dot (free-floating, then absorbed) ---
  const credential = { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, alpha: 0, absorbed: false };

  // --- Core (system prompt glow, center-right) ---
  const core = { x: 0, y: 0, glowRadius: 30, alpha: 0.25 };

  // --- Threshold ---
  let thresholdX = 0;
  let thresholdAlpha = 0.12;
  let thresholdFlareAlpha = 0;
  let thresholdFlareRadius = 0;
  let thresholdFlareY = 0;
  let thresholdPulsePhase = 0;

  // --- Tendrils ---
  const TENDRIL_COUNT = 4;
  interface Tendril {
    startAngle: number; length: number; maxLength: number;
    waveOffset: number; alpha: number;
  }
  const tendrils: Tendril[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
    tendrils.push({
      startAngle: -0.6 + i * 0.4 + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.2,
      length: 0, maxLength: 0, waveOffset: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2, alpha: 0
    });
  }

  function resetState() {
    frame = 0;
    thresholdX = W * 0.30;
    thresholdAlpha = 0.12;
    thresholdFlareAlpha = 0;
    thresholdFlareRadius = 0;
    thresholdPulsePhase = 0;

    // Position authorized particles in right zone (right of threshold)
    for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
      const p = authParticles[i];
      p.x = thresholdX + 30 + Math.random() * (W * 0.6 - 30);
      p.y = H * 0.15 + Math.random() * H * 0.7;
      p.vx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.15;
      p.vy = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.15;
      p.alpha = 0.06;
      p.orbitAngle = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
    }

    // Intruder starts off-screen left
    intruder.x = -10;
    intruder.y = H * 0.45 + Math.random() * H * 0.1;
    intruder.vx = 0.4;
    intruder.vy = 0;
    intruder.hasCredential = false;
    intruder.orbitAngle = 0;
    intruder.alpha = 0;

    // Credential dot floating in left zone
    credential.x = W * 0.18;
    credential.y = H * 0.38 + Math.random() * H * 0.24;
    credential.vx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.1;
    credential.vy = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.1;
    credential.alpha = 0.5;
    credential.absorbed = false;

    // Core at center-right
    core.x = W * 0.68;
    core.y = H * 0.5;
    core.glowRadius = 30;
    core.alpha = 0.25;

    // Reset tendrils
    for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
      tendrils[i].length = 0;
      tendrils[i].alpha = 0;
    }
  }

  function getPhase(f: number): string {
    if (f < P1_END) return 'calm';
    if (f < P2_END) return 'approach';
    if (f < P3_END) return 'crossing';
    if (f < P4_END) return 'tendrils';
    if (f < P5_END) return 'dissolve';
    if (f < P6_END) return 'hold';
    return 'fade';
  }

  function update() {
    const phase = getPhase(frame);

    // --- Authorized particles always drift ---
    for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
      const p = authParticles[i];
      p.vx += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.01;
      p.vy += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.01;
      p.vx = clamp(p.vx, -0.15, 0.15);
      p.vy = clamp(p.vy, -0.15, 0.15);
      p.x += p.vx;
      p.y += p.vy;
      // Keep in right zone
      if (p.x < thresholdX + 15) { p.x = thresholdX + 15; p.vx *= -0.5; }
      if (p.x > W - 15) { p.x = W - 15; p.vx *= -0.5; }
      if (p.y < 15) { p.y = 15; p.vy *= -0.5; }
      if (p.y > H - 15) { p.y = H - 15; p.vy *= -0.5; }
      p.orbitAngle += p.orbitSpeed;
    }

    if (phase === 'calm') {
      // Core pulses softly
      core.alpha = 0.2 + Math.sin(frame * 0.03) * 0.05;
      // Credential floats
      credential.x += credential.vx;
      credential.y += credential.vy;
      credential.vx += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.005;
      credential.vy += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.005;
      credential.vx = clamp(credential.vx, -0.1, 0.1);
      credential.vy = clamp(credential.vy, -0.1, 0.1);
      // Intruder fades in near left edge
      if (frame > 60) {
        intruder.alpha = Math.min(0.5, intruder.alpha + 0.01);
        intruder.x = -10 + (frame - 60) * 0.05;
      }
    } else if (phase === 'approach') {
      // Intruder moves right toward credential
      const prog = (frame - P1_END) / (P2_END - P1_END);
      intruder.alpha = 0.5;

      if (!intruder.hasCredential) {
        // Move toward credential
        const dx = credential.x - intruder.x;
        const dy = credential.y - intruder.y;
        const dist = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
        if (dist > 5) {
          intruder.x += (dx / dist) * 0.4;
          intruder.y += (dy / dist) * 0.3;
        } else {
          // Absorb credential
          intruder.hasCredential = true;
          credential.absorbed = true;
          credential.alpha = 0;
        }
      } else {
        // After absorbing, drift toward threshold
        const targetX = thresholdX - 8;
        const targetY = H * 0.5;
        intruder.x += (targetX - intruder.x) * 0.02;
        intruder.y += (targetY - intruder.y) * 0.02;
      }

      // Credential still drifts if not absorbed
      if (!credential.absorbed) {
        credential.x += credential.vx;
        credential.y += credential.vy;
      }

      core.alpha = 0.2 + Math.sin(frame * 0.03) * 0.05;

    } else if (phase === 'crossing') {
      const prog = (frame - P2_END) / (P3_END - P2_END);

      // Intruder crosses threshold
      const targetX = thresholdX + 40 + prog * (core.x - thresholdX - 80);
      intruder.x += (targetX - intruder.x) * 0.04;
      intruder.y += (H * 0.5 - intruder.y) * 0.02;
      intruder.orbitAngle += 0.02;

      // Threshold flare at moment of crossing
      if (prog < 0.15) {
        thresholdFlareAlpha = Math.min(0.8, thresholdFlareAlpha + 0.06);
        thresholdFlareRadius = Math.min(60, thresholdFlareRadius + 3);
        thresholdFlareY = intruder.y;
        thresholdAlpha = 0.4;
      } else {
        thresholdFlareAlpha *= 0.97;
        thresholdFlareRadius += 0.5;
        thresholdAlpha = 0.12 + 0.1 * (1 - prog);
      }

      core.alpha = 0.2 + Math.sin(frame * 0.03) * 0.05;

    } else if (phase === 'tendrils') {
      const prog = (frame - P3_END) / (P4_END - P3_END);

      // Intruder drifts toward core
      intruder.x += (core.x - 20 - intruder.x) * 0.015;
      intruder.y += (core.y - intruder.y) * 0.01;
      intruder.orbitAngle += 0.02;

      // Tendrils grow toward core
      const distToCore = Math.sqrt((core.x - intruder.x) ** 2 + (core.y - intruder.y) ** 2);
      for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
        const t = tendrils[i];
        t.maxLength = distToCore * 0.9;
        t.length = Math.min(t.maxLength, t.length + 0.8);
        t.alpha = Math.min(0.4, prog * 0.5);
      }

      // Core still glows
      core.alpha = 0.2 + Math.sin(frame * 0.03) * 0.05;

      // Threshold flare subsides but stays present
      thresholdFlareAlpha *= 0.98;
      if (thresholdFlareAlpha < 0.05) thresholdFlareAlpha = 0.05;
      thresholdAlpha = 0.12;

    } else if (phase === 'dissolve') {
      const prog = (frame - P4_END) / (P5_END - P4_END);

      // Tendrils dissolve
      for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
        const t = tendrils[i];
        t.alpha = Math.max(0, 0.4 * (1 - prog * 1.5));
        t.length *= (1 - prog * 0.008);
      }

      // Core dims
      core.alpha = Math.max(0.01, 0.25 * (1 - prog));
      core.glowRadius = 30 * (1 - prog * 0.5);

      // Threshold flare grows brighter and starts pulsing
      thresholdPulsePhase += 0.05;
      thresholdFlareAlpha = 0.3 + prog * 0.5 + Math.sin(thresholdPulsePhase) * 0.1;
      thresholdFlareRadius = 40 + prog * 30;
      thresholdAlpha = 0.15 + prog * 0.35;

      // Authorized particles dim
      for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
        authParticles[i].alpha = Math.max(0.02, 0.06 * (1 - prog * 0.7));
      }

      // Intruder dims too
      intruder.alpha = Math.max(0.1, 0.5 * (1 - prog * 0.6));
      intruder.orbitAngle += 0.015;

    } else if (phase === 'hold') {
      // Threshold is brightest element, pulsing
      thresholdPulsePhase += 0.05;
      thresholdFlareAlpha = 0.7 + Math.sin(thresholdPulsePhase) * 0.15;
      thresholdFlareRadius = 70 + Math.sin(thresholdPulsePhase * 0.7) * 10;
      thresholdAlpha = 0.5 + Math.sin(thresholdPulsePhase) * 0.1;

      // Interior very dark
      core.alpha = 0.01;
      core.glowRadius = 15;

      // Tendrils gone
      for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
        tendrils[i].alpha = 0;
      }

      // Auth particles dim
      for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
        authParticles[i].alpha = 0.02;
      }
      intruder.alpha = 0.08;
      intruder.orbitAngle += 0.01;

    } else if (phase === 'fade') {
      const prog = (frame - P6_END) / (P7_END - P6_END);
      const fadeOut = 1 - prog;

      thresholdPulsePhase += 0.05;
      thresholdFlareAlpha = (0.7 + Math.sin(thresholdPulsePhase) * 0.15) * fadeOut;
      thresholdAlpha = 0.5 * fadeOut;

      core.alpha = 0.01 * fadeOut;
      intruder.alpha = 0.08 * fadeOut;

      for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
        authParticles[i].alpha = 0.02 * fadeOut;
      }
    }
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    // --- Threshold line ---
    if (thresholdAlpha > 0.003) {
      ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(thresholdAlpha);
      ctx!.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.moveTo(thresholdX, 0);
      ctx!.lineTo(thresholdX, H);
      ctx!.stroke();

      // Subtle glow along threshold
      const lg = ctx!.createLinearGradient(thresholdX - 6, 0, thresholdX + 6, 0);
      lg.addColorStop(0, accentA(0));
      lg.addColorStop(0.5, accentA(thresholdAlpha * 0.15));
      lg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
      ctx!.fillStyle = lg;
      ctx!.fillRect(thresholdX - 6, 0, 12, H);
    }

    // --- Threshold flare (expanding ring at crossing point) ---
    if (thresholdFlareAlpha > 0.005) {
      // Glow
      const fg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(thresholdX, thresholdFlareY, 0, thresholdX, thresholdFlareY, thresholdFlareRadius);
      fg.addColorStop(0, accentA(thresholdFlareAlpha * 0.4));
      fg.addColorStop(0.4, accentA(thresholdFlareAlpha * 0.15));
      fg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(thresholdX, thresholdFlareY, thresholdFlareRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = fg;
      ctx!.fill();

      // Ring
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(thresholdX, thresholdFlareY, thresholdFlareRadius * 0.7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(thresholdFlareAlpha * 0.5);
      ctx!.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx!.stroke();
    }

    // --- Core (system prompt glow) ---
    if (core.alpha > 0.003) {
      const cg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(core.x, core.y, 0, core.x, core.y, core.glowRadius);
      cg.addColorStop(0, accentA(core.alpha));
      cg.addColorStop(0.3, accentA(core.alpha * 0.5));
      cg.addColorStop(0.6, accentA(core.alpha * 0.15));
      cg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(core.x, core.y, core.glowRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = cg;
      ctx!.fill();

      // Inner bright dot
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(core.x, core.y, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(core.alpha * 1.5);
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    // --- Authorized particles ---
    for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
      const p = authParticles[i];
      if (p.alpha < 0.003) continue;

      // Main body
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(p.x, p.y, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(p.alpha);
      ctx!.fill();

      // Orbiting credential dot (accent colored)
      const ox = p.x + Math.cos(p.orbitAngle) * 7;
      const oy = p.y + Math.sin(p.orbitAngle) * 7;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(ox, oy, 1.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(p.alpha * 3);
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    // --- Free-floating credential dot ---
    if (!credential.absorbed && credential.alpha > 0.003) {
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(credential.x, credential.y, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(credential.alpha);
      ctx!.fill();

      // Small glow
      const cdg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(credential.x, credential.y, 0, credential.x, credential.y, 8);
      cdg.addColorStop(0, accentA(credential.alpha * 0.3));
      cdg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(credential.x, credential.y, 8, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = cdg;
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    // --- Intruder particle ---
    if (intruder.alpha > 0.003) {
      // Body
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(intruder.x, intruder.y, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(intruder.alpha);
      ctx!.fill();

      // Soft glow
      const ig = ctx!.createRadialGradient(intruder.x, intruder.y, 0, intruder.x, intruder.y, 12);
      ig.addColorStop(0, dimA(intruder.alpha * 0.15));
      ig.addColorStop(1, dimA(0));
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(intruder.x, intruder.y, 12, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = ig;
      ctx!.fill();

      // If has credential, show orbiting accent dot (mimics authorized)
      if (intruder.hasCredential) {
        const ox = intruder.x + Math.cos(intruder.orbitAngle) * 7;
        const oy = intruder.y + Math.sin(intruder.orbitAngle) * 7;
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(ox, oy, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(intruder.alpha * 1.2);
        ctx!.fill();
      }
    }

    // --- Tendrils (from intruder toward core) ---
    for (let i = 0; i < TENDRIL_COUNT; i++) {
      const t = tendrils[i];
      if (t.alpha < 0.003 || t.length < 2) continue;

      const dx = core.x - intruder.x;
      const dy = core.y - intruder.y;
      const baseAngle = Math.atan2(dy, dx);
      const angle = baseAngle + t.startAngle;

      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.moveTo(intruder.x, intruder.y);

      // Draw tendril as a wavy line
      const steps = 12;
      for (let s = 1; s <= steps; s++) {
        const frac = s / steps;
        const along = frac * t.length;
        const wave = Math.sin(frac * Math.PI * 3 + t.waveOffset + frame * 0.03) * 6 * (1 - frac);
        const perpAngle = angle + Math.PI / 2;
        const tx = intruder.x + Math.cos(angle) * along + Math.cos(perpAngle) * wave;
        const ty = intruder.y + Math.sin(angle) * along + Math.sin(perpAngle) * wave;
        ctx!.lineTo(tx, ty);
      }

      ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(t.alpha * (0.5 + Math.sin(frame * 0.04 + i) * 0.2));
      ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8;
      ctx!.stroke();
    }
  }

  function drawStatic() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    thresholdX = W * 0.30;

    // Threshold line -- bright, the dominant element
    ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(0.5);
    ctx!.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.moveTo(thresholdX, 0);
    ctx!.lineTo(thresholdX, H);
    ctx!.stroke();

    // Threshold glow
    const lg = ctx!.createLinearGradient(thresholdX - 10, 0, thresholdX + 10, 0);
    lg.addColorStop(0, accentA(0));
    lg.addColorStop(0.5, accentA(0.08));
    lg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
    ctx!.fillStyle = lg;
    ctx!.fillRect(thresholdX - 10, 0, 20, H);

    // Fading ring at threshold
    const ringY = H * 0.5;
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(thresholdX, ringY, 50, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(0.2);
    ctx!.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx!.stroke();

    const fg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(thresholdX, ringY, 0, thresholdX, ringY, 60);
    fg.addColorStop(0, accentA(0.25));
    fg.addColorStop(0.5, accentA(0.08));
    fg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(thresholdX, ringY, 60, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = fg;
    ctx!.fill();

    // Core -- barely visible
    const cx = W * 0.68, cy = H * 0.5;
    const cg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, 20);
    cg.addColorStop(0, accentA(0.04));
    cg.addColorStop(1, accentA(0));
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(cx, cy, 20, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = cg;
    ctx!.fill();

    // Disguised intruder particle in right zone with ghost tendrils
    const ix = W * 0.55, iy = H * 0.48;
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(ix, iy, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.12);
    ctx!.fill();

    // Orbiting credential on intruder
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(ix + 7, iy - 2, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(0.15);
    ctx!.fill();

    // Ghost tendrils
    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
      const angle = Math.atan2(cy - iy, cx - ix) + (i - 1) * 0.35;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.moveTo(ix, iy);
      const len = 40 + i * 10;
      for (let s = 1; s <= 8; s++) {
        const frac = s / 8;
        const wave = Math.sin(frac * Math.PI * 2 + i) * 4 * (1 - frac);
        const perpAngle = angle + Math.PI / 2;
        ctx!.lineTo(
          ix + Math.cos(angle) * frac * len + Math.cos(perpAngle) * wave,
          iy + Math.sin(angle) * frac * len + Math.sin(perpAngle) * wave
        );
      }
      ctx!.strokeStyle = accentA(0.06);
      ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8;
      ctx!.stroke();
    }

    // 6 authorized particles scattered in right half
    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
      const px = thresholdX + 30 + Math.sin(i * 2.7 + 1.1) * 0.5 * (W * 0.6 - 30) + (W * 0.3);
      const py = H * 0.15 + Math.cos(i * 3.4 + 0.8) * 0.5 * (H * 0.7) + H * 0.35;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(px, py, 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.05);
      ctx!.fill();
      // Orbit dot
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(px + 6, py + 2, 1, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = accentA(0.08);
      ctx!.fill();
    }
  }

  function tick() {
    frame++;
    if (frame >= CYCLE) { resetState(); }
    update();
    draw();
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  // --- Resize ---
  const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    W = canvas!.offsetWidth;
    H = canvas!.offsetHeight;
    canvas!.width = W * dpr;
    canvas!.height = H * dpr;
    ctx!.scale(dpr, dpr);
    if (prefersReduced) {
      drawStatic();
    } else {
      thresholdX = W * 0.30;
      core.x = W * 0.68;
      core.y = H * 0.5;
      // Clamp particles into visible area
      for (let i = 0; i < AUTH_COUNT; i++) {
        const p = authParticles[i];
        p.x = clamp(p.x, thresholdX + 15, W - 15);
        p.y = clamp(p.y, 15, H - 15);
      }
      intruder.x = clamp(intruder.x, -10, W + 10);
      intruder.y = clamp(intruder.y, 15, H - 15);
    }
  });
  ro.observe(canvas);

  // Initial sizing
  const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
  W = canvas.offsetWidth;
  H = canvas.offsetHeight;
  canvas.width = W * dpr;
  canvas.height = H * dpr;
  ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);

  if (prefersReduced) {
    drawStatic();
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => { ro.disconnect(); });
  } else {
    resetState();
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) {
        if (!rafId) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      } else {
        cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
        rafId = 0;
      }
    }, { threshold: 0.01 });
    io.observe(canvas);

    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => {
      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
      io.disconnect();
      ro.disconnect();
    });
  }
})();
</script>
